Many people began making all sorts of conjectures to explain the troublesome layer of mud on the beach. The most widely discussed hypothesis was that the mud came from dredging being carried out at the mouth of the Barra. However, a study by UFRGS technicians, requested by the port authorities, demonstrated that the mud came from a natural phenomenon resulting from movement of deep ocean layers(!).
BUT WHAT NOW?
Meanwhile, we are approaching the end of another year, and the layer of mud remains at Cassino, periodically replenishing itself. Last Sunday, dozens of drivers were surprised by the bed of mud and their cars became stuck. Much effort and help from trucks and people were needed to pull the cars out of Cassino's mud. It is not advisable for laypeople to express opinions contrary to those of technicians. Nevertheless, how can the origin of mud at Cassino be explained by a storm surge, a year after the event?
- COMMENTARY -
Further details we consider important and which support our theory concerning possible "extraterrestrial underwater bases" in the Atlantic Ocean:
1) The stretch of the South Atlantic coast from Balneário do Cassino (the location of the "mud" and the "wave") to the Conceição lighthouse in Bojuru (the location of the "Whale Cemetery") is approximately 60 kilometers long. Thus, considering only the coastline of Rio Grande do Sul, which measures about 500 kilometers, the events occurred very close together, with the obvious exception of the event in Natal, on Parallel 5, which lies in the North Atlantic part;
2) Let us consider the sequence and strange circumstances of the events, for which no satisfactory explanation was found, except for the "earth tremor in Natal," which might indeed have been seismic in nature;
3) It should be remembered that on several occasions "they" have been seen submerging into the sea in their "flying machines," passing beneath ships, and at other times emerging near vessels;
4) Finally, we have reports from reliable sources informing us that extraterrestrials have an underwater base at about 1,500 meters on the Mediterranean seabed, off Taormina in Sicily, Italy, and also a base near Patagonia, Argentina, in the South Atlantic!...
